<!-- Internal note: 2026 rewrite, approved by partner review on 2026-02-14 -->

This Master Service Agreement (this "Agreement" {{def: agreement}}) is entered into on
{{date: 2026-03-01}} between {{party: acme}} and the {{side: clients}}.

> WHEREAS, {{party: acme, label=the Provider}} possesses expertise in software development and
> hosting services; and
>
> WHEREAS, the {{side: clients, label=Clients}} desire to engage the Provider for certain
> technology services;
>
> NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants herein, the parties agree as follows:

# Definitions {#definitions}

"Services" {{def: services}} means the software development, hosting, and support services
described in {{attach: schedule-a, label=Schedule A}}.

"Business Hours" {{def: business-hours}} means 09:00 to 17:00 Central Time on any day that is not
a Saturday, Sunday, or public holiday in the State of Delaware.

"Deliverable" {{def: deliverable}} means any work product the Provider is required to deliver to a
Client under the {{term: agreement}}.

"Acceptance Criteria" {{def:}} means the written criteria against which a {{term: deliverable}} is
tested before promotion to production. The identifier for this definition is omitted and derived
from the term itself (§5.3), producing `acceptance-criteria`.

## Interpretation {#definitions-interpretation}

Defined terms apply equally to their singular and plural forms. References to a *statute* include
any amendment to it. The words `include` and `including` are not limiting.

# Scope of Work {#scope-of-work}

The Provider shall perform the {{term: services}} with the degree of skill and care reasonably
expected of a qualified provider of comparable services.

The Provider shall assign a technical account manager to each Client within
{{duration: 10, unit=D}} of the Effective Date. {#scope-account-manager}

## Change Requests {#scope-changes}

Either side may request a change to the {{term: services}}. A change becomes binding only when:

- the request is submitted in writing {#change-written}
- the Provider confirms the schedule and price impact {#change-impact}
- an authorised representative of each affected party approves it {#change-approval}
  - approval by electronic signature is sufficient
  - approval may not be withheld unreasonably

A change approved under {{ref: change-approval}} amends {{attach: schedule-b, label=Schedule B}}
from the date stated in the approval.

# Payment Terms {#payment-terms}

{{include: includes/payment-terms.lgd}}

# Service Levels {#service-levels}

The Provider shall respond to critical incidents within {{duration: 4, unit=H}} during
{{term: business-hours}} and shall restore service within {{duration: 2, unit=W}} for any
non-critical defect.

| Severity | Response target | Restoration target |
|---|---|---|
| Critical | {{duration: 4, unit=H}} | {{duration: 24, unit=H}} |
| Major | {{duration: 30, unit=MIN}} triage, then next business day | {{duration: 5, unit=D}} |
| Minor | Next business day | {{duration: 2, unit=W}} |

Incidents are tracked by ticket reference, for example {{field: TCK-2026-0417, type=ticket-id}}.

# Intellectual Property {#intellectual-property}

Each {{term: deliverable}} becomes the property of the commissioning Client on payment in full of
the invoice covering it, provided it satisfies the {{term: acceptance-criteria}}.

The Provider retains all rights in its pre-existing materials and in any general know-how acquired
while performing the {{term: services}}. Nothing in this Article transfers rights in any
{{term: deliverable, label=Deliverables}} that remain unpaid.

---

The Provider shall not be liable for any failure caused by a Client's own systems.

# Term and Termination {#term-and-termination}

The {{term: agreement}} commences on {{date: 2026-03-01}} and continues for
{{duration: 24, unit=MO}} unless terminated earlier under this Article.

## Termination for Convenience {#termination-convenience}

Either side may terminate the {{term: agreement}} on {{duration: 90, unit=D}} written notice.

## Termination for Cause {#termination-cause}

A party may terminate immediately if the other party:

- commits a material breach that remains uncured after {{duration: 30, unit=D}} {#cause-breach}
- becomes insolvent or enters liquidation {#cause-insolvency}

Termination under {{ref: cause-breach}} does not affect any accrued right to payment.

# Governing Law and Jurisdiction {#governing-law}

The {{term: agreement}} is governed by the laws of the State of Delaware. The parties submit to
the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of {{placeholder: forum-city}}.

# Notices {#notices}

Notices to the Provider shall be sent to {{party: acme}} at its registered address, marked for the
attention of {{party: acme, label=the Chief Financial Officer}}.

Notices to a Client shall be sent to that Client at the address stated in this
{{term: agreement}}, with a copy to {{party: john-novak}} where the notice concerns
{{attach: exhibit-1}}.
